t** (n_events = 1 in each direction), consistent with the graph's very low repeat ratio (0.035, step_01).\n- The bridge is node 904: 380 events, 308 distinct partners, 4th most active node in the graph (steps 09, 10) and incident to 1769 triangles (step_12). A path through such a hub is essentially guaranteed to exist when time is ignored, so static reachability here is not evidence of a cascade \u2014 it is the expected confounder.\n- Crucially, every tool available to me reports over the **whole horizon [0, 100000]** only; none returns timestamps or restricts to [30939, 69338]. So I cannot check either (a) that the three single events fall inside the query window, or (b) that they occur in the order 60\u219229, 29\u2192904, 904\u2192908 with consecutive gaps \u2264 600.\n- A rough baseline (step_14): for two independent legs, the chance that both gaps fall within 600 units of a ~38400-unit window is ~4\u00d710\u207b\u2075 \u2014 so the temporal constraint is highly restrictive and cannot be assumed satisfied merely because the static path exists.\n\n**Conclusion:** the temporal ordering/latency evidence needed to affirm or refute the cascade is not obtainable; the only positive signal is hub-mediated static connectivity, which is explicitly insufficient.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_64416af4\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [60, 29, 904, 908],\n  \"window\": [30939, 69338],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"60 never contacts 908 directly (step_11). The single static route found is 60->29->904->908, with each leg occurring exactly once (steps 05-08) in a graph with a 3.5% repeat ratio (step_01). The bridge 904 is a top-4 hub (380 events, 308 partners, 1769 triangles; steps 09, 10, 12), so time-ignoring connectivity through it is expected by chance and is a confounder rather than support. No available tool exposes timestamps or restricts to [30939, 69338], so I cannot verify that the three events lie in the window, occur in the required order, or are separated by <=600 units; a baseline estimate (step_14) shows that constraint is very restrictive (~4e-5). Hence the temporal evidence is insufficient to call the cascade present or absent.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 27909, "total_output_tokens": 6362, "total_tokens": 34271, "total_latency_ms": 98862, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}